(* README *)

1 - Summary
    -------

    S003 formalizes a self-contained Rule 30 base semantics and a public
    reduction contract for the center column. It does not prove the
    unconditional center-column nonperiodicity claim; it exposes the
    center-tail-to-window lift obligation as the remaining dependency.

    The semantics are bi-infinite. A row is a function `Z -> bool`, the local
    Rule 30 law is

      Rule30 left center right = xorb left (orb center right),

    the canonical initial row has a single live cell at site `0`, and
    `center_column t` reads site `0` after `t` synchronous steps.

    The certified endpoint is a reduction contract:

      rule30_periodicity_reduction_contract_qed : WITNESS

    where

      WITNESS =
        RULE30_REDUCTION_CONTRACT.

    and

      RULE30_REDUCTION_CONTRACT =
        CENTER_TAIL_TO_WINDOWS_LIFT_OBLIGATION ->
        RULE30_PERIODICITY_CHALLENGE.

    The challenge claim is named separately:

      RULE30_PERIODICITY_CHALLENGE = CENTER_COLUMN_NONPERIODIC.

    The remaining obligation is also named separately:

      CENTER_TAIL_TO_WINDOWS_LIFT_OBLIGATION =
        center_tail_lifts_to_windows.

    Thus S003 proves that the lift obligation is sufficient. The remaining
    public task is to inhabit `center_tail_lifts_to_windows`.


2 - State
    -----

    Closed formal proof of the reduction contract. The terminal assumption
    reports are closed under the global context.


3 - Intuition
    ---------

    The closed part of the proof is row-level. The seeded Rule 30 row at time
    `t` is supported inside `[-t, t]`, and its left edge at site `-t` is always
    live. Therefore rows separated by any positive time lag cannot be identical:
    at time `T + P`, the new left edge is live, while the earlier row at time
    `T` is quiescent there.

    A uniform centered-window tail would force full-row periodicity, since any
    fixed site lies inside some sufficiently large centered window. This
    contradicts the left-edge nonrepetition theorem.

    The remaining premise says that a center-column tail period is not merely
    a radius-zero coincidence: it lifts to all centered windows with the same
    cutoff and period. This lift is deliberately uniform; the same `T` and
    same `P` must work at every radius. Under that premise, any eventual
    center-column period becomes a forbidden uniform centered-window tail.


4 - Tree
    ----

    Stdlib
     ▼
    S003_00_Premises
     ▼
    S003_01_Center_Normalization
     ▼
    S003_96_QED


5 - Files
    -----

    S003_00_Premises.v

      Base semantics, public contract, and closed proof layer. Defines `bit`,
      `row`, `Rule30`, `step_of`, `iterate_step`, `seed_row`, `rule30_row`,
      `center_column`, centered windows, center/window tail periodicity,
      `RULE30_PERIODICITY_CHALLENGE`,
      `CENTER_TAIL_TO_WINDOWS_LIFT_OBLIGATION`,
      `RULE30_REDUCTION_CONTRACT`, and `WITNESS`. It also proves light-cone
      support, live left edge, row nonrepetition at positive lag,
      centered-window-to-row transfer, the Wolfram-form equivalence, the
      certified reduction contract, and the compact lift interface
      `RULE30_LIFT_INTERFACE` / `Rule30ChallengeClosed`. The file also exposes
      the hint databases `rule30_reduction` and `rule30_lift`, with a guard
      showing that `rule30_reduction` does not synthesize the lift obligation.

    S003_01_Center_Normalization.v

      Period-defect normalization interface for the center column. Defines
      pure periods, period defects, defect-free tails, a relational normalizer
      with terminal state `Omega`, finite reachability, period normalization,
      and productive nonperiodicity. Proves that eventual periodicity is
      equivalent to the existence of a positive period whose normalizer reaches
      `Omega`, while keeping productive nonperiodicity separate from negated
      eventual periodicity.

    S003_96_QED.v

      Terminal certification layer. Exposes
      `rule30_periodicity_reduction_contract_qed : WITNESS`,
      `certified_reduction_contract`, and challenge-specialized endpoint
      forms under a supplied lift witness. Records assumption reports.


6 - API
    ---

    Recommended imports:

      Contract and base semantics:
        `From S003 Require Import S003_00_Premises.`

      Certified endpoint:
        `From S003 Require Import S003_96_QED.`

    Public base semantics:

      bit             : Type
      row             : Type
      Rule30          : cellular_rule
      step_of         : cellular_rule -> row -> row
      iterate_step    : cellular_rule -> nat -> row -> row
      seed_row        : row
      rule30_row      : nat -> row
      center_column   : nat -> bit
      centered_line   : nat -> nat -> list bit

    Public contract:

      center_tail_lifts_to_windows            : Prop
      CENTER_TAIL_TO_WINDOWS_LIFT_OBLIGATION  : Prop
      CENTER_COLUMN_NONPERIODIC               : Prop
      RULE30_PERIODICITY_CHALLENGE            : Prop
      UNCONDITIONAL_CHALLENGE_CLAIM           : Prop
      CENTER_COLUMN_NOT_PURELY_PERIODIC       : Prop
      RULE30_REDUCTION_CONTRACT               : Prop
      WITNESS                                 : Prop

    Center normalization:

      period_defect
      is_period_defect
      defect_free_from
      has_defect_from
      center_pure_period
      period_normalizer_step
      normalizer_reaches
      period_normalizes
      period_productive
      CENTER_COLUMN_PRODUCTIVELY_NONPERIODIC
      CENTER_NORMALIZATION_INTERFACE

    Audit facts:

      proved_unconditionally_no_uniform_centered_window_tail :
        forall T P,
          (0 < P)%nat ->
          ~ (forall R t,
              (T <= t)%nat ->
              centered_line R (t + P)%nat = centered_line R t)

      center_nonperiodic_iff_wolfram_form :
        CENTER_COLUMN_NONPERIODIC <-> wolfram_no_eventual_center_period

      period_defect_false_iff_equal :
        forall P t,
          period_defect P t = false <->
          center_column (t + P)%nat = center_column t

      period_defect_true_iff_neq :
        forall P t,
          period_defect P t = true <->
          center_column (t + P)%nat <> center_column t

      pure_period_iff_defect_free_from_zero :
        forall P,
          center_pure_period P <->
          (0 < P)%nat /\ defect_free_from P 0

      tail_period_iff_defect_free_from :
        forall T P,
          center_tail_period T P <->
          (0 < P)%nat /\ defect_free_from P T

      period_normalizes_iff_eventual_period :
        forall P,
          (0 < P)%nat ->
          period_normalizes P <-> exists T, center_tail_period T P

      center_eventually_periodic_iff_some_period_normalizes :
        center_column_eventually_periodic <->
        exists P, (0 < P)%nat /\ period_normalizes P

      productive_nonperiodic_implies_center_nonperiodic :
        CENTER_COLUMN_PRODUCTIVELY_NONPERIODIC ->
        CENTER_COLUMN_NONPERIODIC

      productive_eventual_nonperiodic_implies_productive_not_pure :
        CENTER_COLUMN_PRODUCTIVELY_NONPERIODIC ->
        center_not_purely_periodic_productive

      productive_not_pure_implies_not_purely_periodic :
        center_not_purely_periodic_productive ->
        CENTER_COLUMN_NOT_PURELY_PERIODIC

      certified_center_normalization_interface :
        CENTER_NORMALIZATION_INTERFACE

      challenge_from_lift :
        CENTER_TAIL_TO_WINDOWS_LIFT_OBLIGATION ->
        RULE30_PERIODICITY_CHALLENGE

      wolfram_form_from_lift :
        CENTER_TAIL_TO_WINDOWS_LIFT_OBLIGATION ->
        wolfram_no_eventual_center_period

      reduction_contract_by_auto :
        CENTER_TAIL_TO_WINDOWS_LIFT_OBLIGATION ->
        RULE30_PERIODICITY_CHALLENGE

      wolfram_form_by_auto :
        CENTER_TAIL_TO_WINDOWS_LIFT_OBLIGATION ->
        wolfram_no_eventual_center_period

    Automation:

      rule30_reduction
      rule30_lift

    Lift interface:

      RULE30_LIFT_INTERFACE
      Rule30ChallengeClosed

    Certified endpoint:

      rule30_periodicity_reduction_contract_qed : WITNESS

      certified_reduction_contract :
        RULE30_REDUCTION_CONTRACT

      certified_challenge_under_lift :
        CENTER_TAIL_TO_WINDOWS_LIFT_OBLIGATION ->
        RULE30_PERIODICITY_CHALLENGE

      certified_wolfram_form_under_lift :
        CENTER_TAIL_TO_WINDOWS_LIFT_OBLIGATION ->
        wolfram_no_eventual_center_period

    Secondary corollary:

      center_tail_window_lift_implies_not_purely_periodic :
        center_tail_lifts_to_windows -> CENTER_COLUMN_NOT_PURELY_PERIODIC
